From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: Screenshots, Camera Roll and Saved Pictures known folders

The Pictures subfolders Windows 10 defines, Screenshots, Camera Roll and Saved Pictures, were unknown, so asking for one failed even with KF_FLAG_DONT_VERIFY, which asks for the path whether or not the folder exists yet. OneDrive's folder backup asks for Screenshots while checking the layout of Documents and Desktop, took the failure for an unsupported layout and refused to back them up ("contains other important folders"). The three folders now exist as per-user known folders under Pictures, with their usual names: their path is given without verification, a missing one fails when verified, KF_FLAG_CREATE makes it, and they can be moved like the other per-user folders.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
index 7d6cfc5..86f0d64 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
@@ -2028,7 +2028,35 @@ static const CSIDL_DATA CSIDL_Data[] =
         .name       = L"VideosLibrary",
         .path       = L"Videos.library-ms",
         .parsing    = L"::{031E4825-7B94-4dc3-B131-E946B44C8DD5}\\{491E922F-5643-4af4-A7EB-4E7A138D8174}",
-    }
+    },
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_PICTURES_SUBFOLDERS
+    /* Stained Glass OS 6241: the Pictures subfolders Windows 10 defines (a program asking for one
+     * with KF_FLAG_DONT_VERIFY gets its path though it may not exist yet) */
+    { /* 0x73 */
+        .id         = &FOLDERID_Screenshots,
+        .type       = CSIDL_Type_User,
+        .category   = KF_CATEGORY_PERUSER,
+        .name       = L"Screenshots",
+        .parent     = &FOLDERID_Pictures,
+        .path       = L"Screenshots",
+    },
+    { /* 0x74 */
+        .id         = &FOLDERID_CameraRoll,
+        .type       = CSIDL_Type_User,
+        .category   = KF_CATEGORY_PERUSER,
+        .name       = L"Camera Roll",
+        .parent     = &FOLDERID_Pictures,
+        .path       = L"Camera Roll",
+    },
+    { /* 0x75 */
+        .id         = &FOLDERID_SavedPictures,
+        .type       = CSIDL_Type_User,
+        .category   = KF_CATEGORY_PERUSER,
+        .name       = L"SavedPictures",
+        .parent     = &FOLDERID_Pictures,
+        .path       = L"Saved Pictures",
+    },
+#endif
 };
 
 static int csidl_from_id( const KNOWNFOLDERID *id )
